{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/772604-silver-fang-as-a-modern-csar-possible-alternate-history","id":772604,"title":"Silver Fang As a Modern Csar (Possible alternate history)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-23T16:17:51-08:00","id":772604,"title":"Silver Fang As a Modern Csar (Possible alternate history)","content":"Noticed a LOT of nostalgia from the fangs for old russian royalty... any thoughts on them (Possibly ripping the veil to shreds possibly working through proxies) reconquering russia<br /> <br /> I got the impression its something a LOT of fangs would like to see happen...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T16:43:14-08:00","id":772628,"title":"","content":"Doubtful. They are not patterned after the Tzars. They are patterned after the pre-Tzarist kings and princes of slavic history interspread with hefty doses of Slavic Mythology. They have more in common with the Fianna and the Get as how they treat their kingly heritage (they are glorious Moon King heroes of the people) than the Russian Empire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T18:10:06-08:00","id":772685,"title":"","content":"Silver Fangs have two big distinctions - the first is that many of their kinfolk are descended from the old human nobility, and the second is that their lupus are from the Eurasian forests and taiga. The two naturally come together in Russia. Russia was the last absolutist monarchy in the world, and the drama of the Russian Revolution adds to that nostalgia for a lost world.<br /> <br /> However, I would not say that translates into having an actual agenda to restore the Russian monarchy among the humans. The more reactionary members of the tribe may wish to see a return of a hierarchical society in general, but that is obviously unrealistic at this point.<br /> <br /> I am sure there are some Silver Fang kinfolk involved in the various revivalists movement in Russia that adores the pre-Communist Russian past, but no one is pushing for a Romanov restoration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/772604-silver-fang-as-a-modern-csar-possible-alternate-history?p=772628#post772628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are not patterned after the Tzars. They are patterned after the pre-Tzarist kings and princes of slavic history interspread with hefty doses of Slavic Mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know there are a lot of history buffs who play WoD, but the distinction between the nobility of Kievan Rus (including the Grand Prince of Moscow), the Tsar of Russia, and the Russian Emperor probably isn't known to many players.<br /> <br /> Also, the game sourcebooks make an explicit connection with the tribe's kinfolk and the Romanov dynasty. Personally, I agree with you it's best to push those ties way into the past and not emphasize real world figures involvement in the supernatural. However, that was not how the game originally developed, and there are lots of ties.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T18:40:05-08:00","id":772697,"title":"","content":"Honestly, in their original concept, I fully believe they were meant to be tzars. However, by revised, it would be fixed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T01:22:21-08:00","id":772871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/772604-silver-fang-as-a-modern-csar-possible-alternate-history?p=772685#post772685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know there are a lot of history buffs who play WoD, but the distinction between the nobility of Kievan Rus (including the Grand Prince of Moscow), the Tsar of Russia, and the Russian Emperor probably isn't known to many players.<br /> <br /> Also, the game sourcebooks make an explicit connection with the tribe's kinfolk and the Romanov dynasty. Personally, I agree with you it's best to push those ties way into the past and not emphasize real world figures involvement in the supernatural. However, that was not how the game originally developed, and there are lots of ties.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is a shame. Mythology and History are great resources for game like Werewolf. The Tzarist thing came from a cluelessness of the early writers who probably didn't do a lot of research on the topic. What they did with Baba Yaga is one of the most galling examples of that. Just because a sin of an early edition matches the Fangs with something that's pretty much off key for them as a historical group doesn't mean that we need to reinforce that stereotype.<br /> <br /> Of course there are Fangs among the Russian nobility, but it's important to see where they came from. They resonate perfectly with the cultural heroes such as the Bogatyr, Vasilissa and Tsarevitch Ivan (who has nothing to do with Tzars). They are the kings of the people.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T05:41:40-08:00","id":773000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/772604-silver-fang-as-a-modern-csar-possible-alternate-history#post772604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Noticed a LOT of nostalgia from the fangs for old russian royalty... any thoughts on them (Possibly ripping the veil to shreds possibly working through proxies) reconquering russia<br /> <br /> I got the impression its something a LOT of fangs would like to see happen...</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking about this recently as well, maybe has something to do with first snowfall here, so I started looking into any sort of modern monarchist movements in Russia, and in the rest of Europe where the Fang Houses originated. I found this book: <a href=\"http://www.worldcat.org/title/black-hundred-the-rise-of-the-extreme-right-in-russia/oclc/26974540&amp;referer=brief_results\" target=\"_blank\">Black Hundred: the Rise of the Extreme Right in Russia</a>, which I plan on reading soon, and thought it might be useful. For the most part I agree with later posters that the Silver Fangs of Clan Crescent Moon have more connection to the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rurik_dynasty\" target=\"_blank\">Rurikids</a>, than the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House_of_Romanov\" target=\"_blank\">Romanovs</a>.<br /> <br /> I feel that the connection to the Romanovs fit to a degree, in 1st edition as well, as Russia remained feudal for a much longer period than other European nations and the general, popular impression is that the Romanovs themselves were doddering, fairly inbred (as were most of the European royals), and resting on the laurels of generations long past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":1813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","user":"grimjaws","date":". 11-24-2015, 08:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T06:10:58-08:00","id":773035,"title":"","content":"hmmmn thoughts on the idea of Silver fangs trying to bring back the Csars?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T06:28:05-08:00","id":773053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/772604-silver-fang-as-a-modern-csar-possible-alternate-history?p=773035#post773035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hmmmn thoughts on the idea of Silver fangs trying to bring back the Csars?</div> </div> </div> </div>Might as well try to bring back the biplane and the steam powered paddle ship while you are at it, the concept of people going back to a monarchy system of government really won't work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T06:44:17-08:00","id":773062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/772604-silver-fang-as-a-modern-csar-possible-alternate-history?p=772685#post772685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know there are a lot of history buffs who play WoD, but the distinction between the nobility of Kievan Rus (including the Grand Prince of Moscow), the Tsar of Russia, and the Russian Emperor probably isn't known to many players.<br /> <br /> Also, the game sourcebooks make an explicit connection with the tribe's kinfolk and the Romanov dynasty. Personally, I agree with you it's best to push those ties way into the past and not emphasize real world figures involvement in the supernatural. However, that was not how the game originally developed, and there are lots of ties.</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially as the line of Rurik died with Ivan IV and his son Feodor, who were the rulers before the Romanovs. Rurik was a fascinating figure, since he was a viking that, according to legend, was so impressive a warrior and leader, the Slavs begged him to be their Grand Prince. Clearly a Silver Fang.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T06:48:11-08:00","id":773064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/772604-silver-fang-as-a-modern-csar-possible-alternate-history?p=773035#post773035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hmmmn thoughts on the idea of Silver fangs trying to bring back the Csars?</div> </div> </div> </div>Which Tsars? You're talking about Emperors. And Emperor is a a title, and what we think of as Russia was led by multiple different legacies that are not exactly related or consistant with each other. The Romanovs were probably the least impressive of the lot (probably because we actually have better historical records on them). Mind you, the most popular Romanovs of fiction and history are not even Romanovs by blood!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8760,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","user":"Cogliostro","date":". 11-24-2015, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T07:02:23-08:00","id":773072,"title":"","content":"As a purely plot idea the resurrection of the monarchy even as a symbolic gesture has merit. The Orthodox church currently wields a great deal of political clout and an unholy alliance of Garou, Orthodox, and Vampires perhaps Tzismice could make an interesting story. <br /> I don't think I would run it, there are more pressing issues that could be addressed in a Russian chronicle. The return of a dictatorship government, the suppression of dissidents, the annexation of the Crimerian peninsula as well as the continued hunting of wolves by the state could all be used as a chronicle that would be more compelling in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":293,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","user":"lncbill","date":".  missed a d. 11-24-2015, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T07:16:01-08:00","id":773084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/772604-silver-fang-as-a-modern-csar-possible-alternate-history?p=773035#post773035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hmmmn thoughts on the idea of Silver fangs trying to bring back the Csars?</div> </div> </div> </div>My knee jerk reaction would be to say yes there are some Silver Fangs looking to bring back the Tsars. After I look back through <i>Rage Across Russia</i> and read <i>Black Hundred</i> I can provide some better thoughts as to the whos and hows.<br /> <br /> Another thing to consider is just how closely tied are the Silver Fangs to the Tsars and other noble Houses in Europe. If it is all direct or immediate relations then the two Houses in the Americas will be seen that much more as outsiders as the rich Americans that Wyrmfoe and Unbreakable Hearth are linked too did not descend from noble Europeans. Some eventually married in the nobility of Europe, as the Million Dollar American Princesses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T10:01:31-08:00","id":773218,"title":"","content":"Both Houses associated primarily with the U.S. and Canada began to come into prominence in the Middle Ages per Werewolf the Dark Ages the revised version. So more than likely they originally were in the rising mercantile class something that was mentioned that Conquering Claw was attempting as well until they ran into the Giovanni. Austere Howl is tied to the old French and German noble and royal lines (British monarchy as well since at one point the current House of Windsor was the ruling family of Hanover). Gleaming Eye seems to be tied with Scotland, Normans, and old Celtic lines. I would guess the Lost House features in the Silver Crown saga was tied to the Anglo-Saxon lines. Wise Heart has ties with Egypt, and the Middle East perhaps related to the Turkish invaders. Blood Red Crest is tied to India and would I imagine be tied to both the Brahmin and Warrior castes. The Ice Pack seem to be an all Lupus house. I know I'm missing a few of the Houses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T11:09:23-08:00","id":773258,"title":"","content":"Ah, writing inconsistencies. In the Silver Fang tribebook (p.36, p.38 Revised), Gleaming Eye comes from &quot;Northern Europe ... France, Germany, and Scandinavia.&quot; It is also linked to the Anglo-Saxons kings in Britain. I think that the Fangs picked up something from the Fenrir in Central Europe by maintaining the elective monarchy of the HRE. Now why did that not spread to other Houses? I would guess for a long while the Houses did not necessarily have terribly close ties to each other, though I am not sold on that idea completely.<br /> <br /> Austere Howl I see more as having come to England with the Bastard and his men (confirmed by Dark Ages Werewolf), and the eventual drawing in of the Saxe-Coburg and Gotha family as an attempt by either Austere Howl to revitalize its blood or an attempt by Gleaming Eye to win back the island, this is my own speculation as all the entries I found in the tribebooks talk about the current affairs of Austere Howl only.<br /> <br /> Wyrmfoe originated in England, France, and Spain (original tribebook) or France, Spain, and Holland, spreading to England (Revised tribebook) during the Inquisition.<br /> <br /> Unbreakable Hearth came from a Spain, Italy, and France (original tribebook) or France, Spain, Switzerland, and Hungary (Revised tribebook). Kind of an odd hodgepodge House in my opinion. I agree with Incbill that both Wyrmfoe and Unbreakable Hearth could very well be associate with more &quot;middle class&quot; families than the older Houses.<br /> <br /> So I think I'll stick with the idea that Wyrmfoe and Unbreakable Hearth are not from old, noble families. Also that the interrelations of the older Houses is a relatively recent phenomenon. I can also see the real strongholds of the Fangs in the more recent past being Russia and Prussia, both holding onto feudal models of governance for much longer than the rest of Europe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":1813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","user":"grimjaws","date":". 11-24-2015, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}